      "math_academy_id": "e-5879",
      "problem": "Solve $2x^3+3x^2-8x-12=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "We proceed to factor the left side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-8x-12 & = \\\\ (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})-(8x+12) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(2x+3)-4(2x+3) & = \\\\ (2x+3)\\cdot {x}^{2}-(2x+3)\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ (2x+3)({x}^{2}-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(2x+3)(x^2-4) = 0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(2x+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-2, \\; -\\dfrac{3}{2}, \\; 2.$",
